{
  "info": {
    "name": "Google Search Console API",
    "description": "Search Console API v3 (sites, sitemaps, search analytics) plus URL Inspection v1.\n\n## Auth\nEvery request sends `Bearer {{accessToken}}`. Two ways to fill it:\n\n**A. Run request 1.** Needs the OAuth client id, client secret and refresh token of a\nGoogle user with access to the properties - the same pattern as `google-business/` in\nthis repo, where the refresh token no longer expires because the OAuth app is published.\nRequest 1 saves the access token into the collection automatically; it lasts ~1 hour.\n\n**B. Paste one in.** `gcloud auth print-access-token` for a user account, or a token for\na service account that has been added under Settings -> Users and permissions. Note that\na service account must be added **per property** - Search Console has no org-wide access.\n\nScopes: `.../auth/webmasters.readonly` to read, `.../auth/webmasters` to submit or delete.\n\n## The one gotcha\n`siteUrl` goes in the URL *path*, so it must be percent-encoded. A collection pre-request\nscript derives `{{siteUrlEnc}}` and `{{feedpathEnc}}` for you - edit only the readable\n`siteUrl` and `feedpath` variables. Un-encoded values are the usual cause of a 404 here.\n\nProperty identity is exact: `https://superhairpieces.ca/` (trailing slash),\n`https://www.superhairpieces.com/` (www is a separate property from non-www), or\n`sc-domain:superhairpieces.ca` for a Domain property.\n\n## Superhairpieces properties\nImport the companion environment file for all six storefronts. `.com` is **www**; `.ca`,\n`.nl`, `.fr`, `.es` and `.de` are non-www. Every store serves a BigCommerce-generated\nsitemap index at `/xmlsitemap.php`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// siteUrl sits in the URL *path*, so it must be percent-encoded. This is the",
          "// single most common cause of a 404 on this API: /sites/https://x.com/ is not",
          "// a valid path - it has to be /sites/https%3A%2F%2Fx.com%2F.",
          "// Encoded copies are derived here so you only ever edit the readable variables.",
          "const siteUrl = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"siteUrl\") || \"\";",
          "const feedpath = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"feedpath\") || \"\";",
          "",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"siteUrlEnc\", encodeURIComponent(siteUrl));",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"feedpathEnc\", encodeURIComponent(feedpath));",
          "",
          "if (siteUrl && !siteUrl.startsWith(\"sc-domain:\") && !siteUrl.endsWith(\"/\")) {",
          "  console.warn(\"siteUrl has no trailing slash. A URL-prefix property is stored \"",
          "    + \"WITH one and the API matches it exactly, e.g. https://superhairpieces.ca/\");",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Get Access Token (refresh token)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token",
          "path": [
            "token"
          ],
          "protocol": "https",
          "host": [
            "oauth2",
            "googleapis",
            "com"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Exchanges a long-lived refresh token for a ~1 hour access token and saves it to {{accessToken}}. Form-encoded, which is what Google's token endpoint expects.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "urlencoded",
          "urlencoded": [
            {
              "key": "client_id",
              "value": "{{clientId}}",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "key": "client_secret",
              "value": "{{clientSecret}}",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "key": "refresh_token",
              "value": "{{refreshToken}}",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "key": "grant_type",
              "value": "refresh_token",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Saves the access token so every other request in the collection can use it.",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "if (body.access_token) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", body.access_token);",
              "  console.log(\"accessToken saved, expires in \" + body.expires_in + \"s\");",
              "}",
              "pm.test(\"200 OK\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Sites - List properties",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webmasters/v3/sites",
          "path": [
            "webmasters",
            "v3",
            "sites"
          ],
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Every property this credential can see, with its permission level. Run this first: the console output gives you the exact siteUrl strings to paste into the siteUrl variable, which removes all guesswork about www and trailing slashes.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{accessToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"200 OK\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "",
              "// Prints the exact siteUrl strings to paste into the siteUrl variable. Domain",
              "// properties come back as sc-domain:example.com; URL-prefix properties keep",
              "// their scheme, host and trailing slash - and www is a DIFFERENT property.",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "(body.siteEntry || []).forEach(function (s) {",
              "  console.log(s.siteUrl + \"   [\" + s.permissionLevel + \"]\");",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Sites - Get one",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webmasters/v3/sites/{{siteUrlEnc}}",
          "path": [
            "webmasters",
            "v3",
            "sites",
            "{{siteUrlEnc}}"
          ],
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Confirms a property exists and what permission level you hold on it.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{accessToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Sitemaps - List for a property",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webmasters/v3/sites/{{siteUrlEnc}}/sitemaps",
          "path": [
            "webmasters",
            "v3",
            "sites",
            "{{siteUrlEnc}}",
            "sitemaps"
          ],
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "THE check for 'is my sitemap submitted'. An empty response means nothing is registered on this property. Per sitemap you get path, lastDownloaded, isPending, errors, warnings and submitted/indexed counts; the test script prints one line each.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{accessToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"200 OK\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "",
              "// An empty body is the answer people miss: it means NO sitemap is registered on",
              "// this property. Google may still crawl one it auto-discovered from robots.txt,",
              "// but nothing is registered here - and the registered ones are what Bing",
              "// Webmaster Tools carries over when you import from Search Console.",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "const feeds = body.sitemap || [];",
              "",
              "if (feeds.length === 0) {",
              "  console.log(\"NO sitemaps registered on \" + pm.collectionVariables.get(\"siteUrl\"));",
              "} else {",
              "  feeds.forEach(function (f) {",
              "    const web = (f.contents || []).filter(function (c) { return c.type === \"web\"; })[0] || {};",
              "    console.log([",
              "      f.path,",
              "      \"lastDownloaded=\" + (f.lastDownloaded || \"never\"),",
              "      \"pending=\" + Boolean(f.isPending),",
              "      \"errors=\" + (f.errors || 0),",
              "      \"warnings=\" + (f.warnings || 0),",
              "      \"submitted=\" + (web.submitted || 0),",
              "      \"indexed=\" + (web.indexed || 0)",
              "    ].join(\"  \"));",
              "  });",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Sitemaps - Get one",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webmasters/v3/sites/{{siteUrlEnc}}/sitemaps/{{feedpathEnc}}",
          "path": [
            "webmasters",
            "v3",
            "sites",
            "{{siteUrlEnc}}",
            "sitemaps",
            "{{feedpathEnc}}"
          ],
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Detail for a single sitemap, including per-content-type counts. For a sitemap index this reports the index itself; its child sitemaps appear separately in request 4.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{accessToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Sitemaps - Submit",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webmasters/v3/sites/{{siteUrlEnc}}/sitemaps/{{feedpathEnc}}",
          "path": [
            "webmasters",
            "v3",
            "sites",
            "{{siteUrlEnc}}",
            "sitemaps",
            "{{feedpathEnc}}"
          ],
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Registers a sitemap. No request body, returns 204, and is idempotent - re-submitting an existing sitemap is harmless. Needs the read-write webmasters scope. This is the API equivalent of typing the path into the 'Add a new sitemap' box.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{accessToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Sitemaps - Delete",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webmasters/v3/sites/{{siteUrlEnc}}/sitemaps/{{feedpathEnc}}",
          "path": [
            "webmasters",
            "v3",
            "sites",
            "{{siteUrlEnc}}",
            "sitemaps",
            "{{feedpathEnc}}"
          ],
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Unregisters a sitemap; returns 204. Does not stop Google crawling one it auto-discovered from robots.txt.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{accessToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "8. Search Analytics - Query",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webmasters/v3/sites/{{siteUrlEnc}}/searchAnalytics/query",
          "path": [
            "webmasters",
            "v3",
            "sites",
            "{{siteUrlEnc}}",
            "searchAnalytics",
            "query"
          ],
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Clicks, impressions, CTR and average position. Data starts ~2 days back, which is why endDate is not today. rowLimit maxes at 25000; page with startRow. Add a dimensionFilterGroups block to filter by country, device or query.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{accessToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"startDate\": \"{{startDate}}\",\n  \"endDate\": \"{{endDate}}\",\n  \"dimensions\": [\n    \"query\",\n    \"page\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": \"web\",\n  \"rowLimit\": 100,\n  \"startRow\": 0\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "9. URL Inspection - Inspect a URL",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/urlInspection/index:inspect",
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "urlInspection",
            "index:inspect"
          ],
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Index status for one URL: coverage verdict, the canonical Google chose, last crawl, mobile usability, and which sitemaps reference it. Quota is tight (~2000/day) so this is for spot checks, not bulk auditing. inspectionUrl must sit inside siteUrl.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{accessToken}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"inspectionUrl\": \"{{inspectUrl}}\",\n  \"siteUrl\": \"{{siteUrl}}\",\n  \"languageCode\": \"en-US\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://searchconsole.googleapis.com",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Also served at https://www.googleapis.com - same API."
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Filled automatically by request 1, or paste one in. ~1 hour lifetime."
    },
    {
      "key": "clientId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "OAuth client id of the developer-owned project. Request 1 only."
    },
    {
      "key": "clientSecret",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "OAuth client secret. Request 1 only - do not commit a real value."
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Refresh token for the Google user managing the properties. Request 1 only - do not commit a real value."
    },
    {
      "key": "siteUrl",
      "value": "https://superhairpieces.ca/",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Exact property id. Trailing slash for URL-prefix properties; www is a separate property; sc-domain:example.com for a Domain property."
    },
    {
      "key": "siteUrlEnc",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Derived by the pre-request script. Do not edit."
    },
    {
      "key": "feedpath",
      "value": "https://superhairpieces.ca/xmlsitemap.php",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Full sitemap URL. BigCommerce serves a sitemap index at /xmlsitemap.php."
    },
    {
      "key": "feedpathEnc",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Derived by the pre-request script. Do not edit."
    },
    {
      "key": "startDate",
      "value": "2026-09-01",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Search Analytics range start, YYYY-MM-DD."
    },
    {
      "key": "endDate",
      "value": "2026-10-19",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Range end. Keep ~2 days behind today; recent data is not final."
    },
    {
      "key": "inspectUrl",
      "value": "https://superhairpieces.ca/products/hook-needle.html",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "URL to inspect. Must be inside siteUrl."
    }
  ]
}